course: dictionary
lesson: 948
title: Bloodhound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dog's nose can be a superpower. «A bloodhound follows the trail of a missing person for miles.» A bloodhound is a large dog with a very good sense of smell, so it can follow a trail that people cannot see or smell.
explain: The word has two meanings. The first is the dog, which has long droopy ears and loose wrinkled skin. The second, informal meaning is a person, like a detective, who is very good at finding things out. When a word has more than one meaning, read the sentence and check which one fits.
explain: Context shows you which meaning to use. «The police brought in a bloodhound to sniff out the trail.» Police and trail tell you this is the dog. Now read: «Ella is a bloodhound when it comes to finding lost keys.» This time it is a person, because a dog cannot be good at finding lost keys in the way that a clever person can.
fact: A bloodhound is a large dog with a very good sense of smell.
fact: Its long droopy ears and loose wrinkled skin are part of how it looks.
fact: Bloodhounds are used to track missing people or escaped prisoners.
fact: «Bloodhound» can also mean a person, like a detective, who is very good at finding things out.
fact: «A bear's sense of smell is one of the best of any animal, said to be several times better than a bloodhound's.» So a bloodhound has a great nose, but some animals have even better noses.
exercise: «A bear's sense of smell is said to be several times better than a bloodhound's.» Which animal has the better sense of smell? | A rabbit | *A bear | A cat | A pony
exercise: What is a bloodhound? | A kind of bird that sings at night | A fast car used by police | A small cat that climbs trees | *A large dog with a very good sense of smell
exercise: Lola says, «My cousin is a bloodhound at finding lost things.» What does she mean? | *Her cousin is very good at finding things out | Her cousin has long droopy ears | Her cousin lost all the keys | Her cousin is afraid of dogs
test: «The police used a bloodhound to sniff out the trail.» What does sniff out mean here? | Run away quickly | Ignore it completely | *Find something by smell or careful searching | Blow the nose hard
test: Which feature of a bloodhound is described as long and droopy? | Its paws | Its tail | *Its ears | Its teeth
exam: «The school bloodhound found the missing ruler in ten minutes.» What does bloodhound mean in this sentence? | *A person who is very good at finding things out | A dog that cannot smell | A large dog with long droopy ears | A sad, tired puppy
